The Laboratory of Things (corona): a hemispherical geodesic tensile structure in black metal and reflecting glass.
Written by Gemini CLI (Gemini 3.8 Flash, subscription) on 23/10/2026, task T19.
Box: 14 × 14 × 8 tiles, 112 × 112 × 64 voxels, 8 voxels per tile.
Key letters:
  O = door (letter O, name "porta", at the centre x=56, y=98, z=0..16, inner hall empty for 18 voxels)
  F = sign ("IL LABORATORIO DELLE COSE", copper neon d89a6a with a steady glow on the front totem to the left)
  P = dark matte plate for the totem of the sign
  M = primary black metal (tensile structure and ribs)
  m = dark secondary metal (inner machinery and pillars)
  C = graphite concrete of the base and paving
  S = light steel / tensile joints / cables
  V = dark reflecting glass
  v = bands of bluish reflection on the glass
  n = thin copper neon for joints and rings (glow)
  N = bright copper neon for the portal and the core (glow)
  x = temporary buffer for the animation (hidden)
Pulsing phases of the copper (1..8):
  1..8 = continuous gradient of 8 phases (from 844422 to f2b07c) with a soft wave, the breathing of the laboratory.
Tensile structure and Dome:
  Geodesic hemispherical dome (diameter 80 voxels, z=0..40) with a lattice of lozenges and triangles in black metal,
  dark reflecting glass panels with horizontal and diagonal reflections, outer tension pillars and steel cables.
Tunnel forward block:
  Entrance tunnel jutting out to the south (y=74..98) with a cybernetic portal, a copper neon frame and a free entrance space.
Sign totem:
  Cybernetic monolith on the left side (x=4..48, y=102..107, z=0..29) with a dark matte plate, rear tie rods and pixel neon writing
  "IL LABORATORIO DELLE COSE" on three lines, perfectly centred and readable from the avenue.
Inner laboratory:
  A through hall, the central chamber of matter synthesis with a containment cylinder and a pulsing copper plasma core.
Animation "sintesi" (8 frames):
  A continuous energy wave flowing through the geodesic rings, the tensile cables and the central core.
-->
